# Individual: coho:COHO_0001676 (obsolete EAS)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0001676 coho:COHO_0001677)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0001676 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. EAS, the PGS Catalog cohort id used for the type 2 diabetes score PGS000020 (Läll et al. 2016), is the DIAGRAM consortium’s EAS, which its 2012 meta-analysis (PMID:22885922) describes as funded by the British Heart Foundation (RG/98002) and genotyped in Edinburgh, the funding of the Edinburgh Artery Study (PMC5841831: EAS (Edinburgh Artery Study). EAS is funded by the British Heart Foundation (Programme Grant RG/98002)); the Catalog also lists the study under its own name as EAS-Edinburgh. Replaced by COHO:0001677, Edinburgh Artery Study, which carries the acronym EAS. Found by the review of 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0001676 "obsolete EAS"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0001676 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

