# Individual: coho:COHO_0001859 (obsolete Hussman Institute of Human Genomics)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0001859 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. HIHG is the Hussman Institute for Human Genomics of the University of Miami (formerly the Miami Institute for Human Genomics). In the PGS Catalog's source paper the id labels the institute's Parkinson's disease GWAS sample, a genotyping set of unrelated cases gathered by the 13 ascertainment centres of the PD Genetics Collaboration and the Udall Parkinson Disease Center of Excellence core, with spouse and friend controls (PMID:20070850, PMC2853717). It is a GWAS sample assembled from those collections under the institute's name, not a collection with a name of its own. If a term is ever wanted, the named collection behind it would be the PD Genetics Collaboration (Scott et al. 2001) or the Udall center's collection, not HIHG. No COHO term or review name matches; the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium (COHO:0001108) and the Ashkenazi Jewish Dataset (COHO:0001283) are separate datasets of the same meta-analysis. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0001859 "obsolete Hussman Institute of Human Genomics"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0001859 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

