# Individual: coho:COHO_0001912 (obsolete Infanta Leonor University Hospital (Madrid, Spain))

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0001912 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog's full name for ILUH, 'Infanta Leonor University Hospital (Madrid, Spain)', is wrong: in the CIMBA papers the Catalog curated, ILUH is Iceland's Landspitali University Hospital. ILUH is the PGS Catalog's id for the BRCA1/BRCA2 pathogenic-variant carriers contributed to CIMBA (COHO:0000901) by Landspitali University Hospital in Reykjavik, Iceland (PMID:28448241, 34320204, 32665703, 36203093); the Catalog's expansion 'Infanta Leonor University Hospital (Madrid, Spain)' is an error. The sample has no name of its own beyond the hospital, so, like the other institution-named CIMBA sites the review decided (MSKCC, UPENN, BRICOH, Chicago, FCCC, OUH, and E522 ICO in this batch), it is not a cohort. It is not the deCODE genetics Icelandic cohort (COHO:0000428): CIMBA lists it as a clinic-based site sample of mutation carriers. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0001912 "obsolete Infanta Leonor University Hospital (Madrid, Spain)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0001912 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

