# Individual: coho:COHO_0001931 (obsolete Charles R Bronfman Institute for Personalized Medicine - IPM / BioBank Genome Wide Association Study of Cardiovascular, Renal and Metabolic Phenotypes)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0001931 coho:COHO_0000424)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0001931 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. IPM is the Charles Bronfman Institute for Personalized Medicine at Mount Sinai, and the PGS id denotes its BioMe Biobank (the catalog's long name is the IPM BioBank GWAS), which COHO already has as COHO:0000424 BioMe Biobank (it already carries the synonyms 'IPM Biobank' and 'Institute for Personalized Medicine (IPM) BioMe Biobank Project'). Add the PGS id IPM as an acronym and the catalog's full name as a synonym; no other COHO term uses the acronym IPM. The placeholder COHO:0001931 is a duplicate. The CARDIoGRAMplusC4D sub-sample tags IPM-EurAmer, IPM-AfrAmer, IPM-HispAmer (and IPM_EA, IPM_AA, IPM_HA) are ancestry subsets of the same biobank; they could be added as synonyms if the curator wants every tag, but neither catalog uses them as ids. Replaced by COHO:0000424 (BioMe Biobank), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0001931 "obsolete Charles R Bronfman Institute for Personalized Medicine - IPM / BioBank Genome Wide Association Study of Cardiovascular, Renal and Metabolic Phenotypes"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0001931 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

