# Individual: coho:COHO_0002186 (obsolete North Shore University Health System)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002186 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The one id is used for two unrelated samples from the same health system, a CIMBA contributing centre and an active-surveillance prostate cancer series, neither with a study name. NSUHS is the PGS Catalog's id for NorthShore University HealthSystem, Evanston, Illinois, USA, as a site, used for two unrelated samples: (1) the BRCA1/BRCA2 pathogenic-variant carriers NorthShore contributed to CIMBA (CIMBA's code NORTHSHORE; PMID:32665703, 28346442), and (2) 432 prostate cancer patients of European ancestry on active surveillance at NorthShore, evaluated for a prostate cancer PRS together with Johns Hopkins patients (PMID:33956350, PSS001140). Neither sample has a study name or a design of its own beyond the institution ('separate active surveillance studies conducted at ... NorthShore University HealthSystem'), so the id denotes an institution, not a named cohort. The CIMBA carriers are covered by CIMBA (COHO:0000901). It is not the Polish Breast Cancer Study (COHO:0000930), which the triage matched only through a shared line of the ethics list. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002186 "obsolete North Shore University Health System"@en)
