# Individual: coho:COHO_0002199 (obsolete Oncology Department of Zaragoza Hospital)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002199 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. ODZH is the PGS Catalog's id for the Spanish case-control material that deCODE genetics' multi-population cancer GWAS used as a replication group: cancer patients (lung, ovarian and thyroid cancer in the papers read) recruited from the Oncology Department of Zaragoza Hospital, with controls who attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza for other conditions (PMID:21303977, 28195142, 21964575). The papers call it only 'the Spanish study population' or 'Zaragoza, Spain', with case recruitment differing by cancer; it has no study name and no design of its own beyond the hospital, so the id denotes a site, not a named cohort (like LUHR, E651, the Landspitali material in the same deCODE papers). No COHO term covers it. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002199 "obsolete Oncology Department of Zaragoza Hospital"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002199 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

