# Individual: coho:COHO_0002296 (obsolete Program in Sleep at Emory University)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002296 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog id PSEU is not attached to any score or sample set in the Catalog's current data (REST /cohort/PSEU returns nothing; absent from cohort_papers.json), so the Catalog paper that used it could not be read; the identification of the sample rests on the name, which matches the restless legs syndrome sample of Emory University's Department of Neurology and Program in Sleep. The Program in Sleep at Emory University is a clinical sleep programme in Atlanta (United States), not a study. The only sample of that name found is the restless legs syndrome case-control collection of the Department of Neurology and Program in Sleep, which the RLS GWAS PMID:33239738 calls just 'Emory cohort' / 'US Emory' (1417 subjects, 696 RLS cases): a clinic's sample with no study name of its own, like the other place-named samples judged not to be cohorts (e.g. KULEUVEN, Toronto). The Catalog id presumably denotes that collection in an RLS polygenic score paper that could not be identified. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002296 "obsolete Program in Sleep at Emory University"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002296 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

