# Individual: coho:COHO_0002403 (obsolete The Spanish study (University Hospital of Bellvitge, Hospital of Leon))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002403 coho:COHO_0000585)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002403 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The paper's supplement (the likely source of the Catalog's full name) could not be downloaded, even through the watcher; the identification rests on the hospitals named, the paper's acknowledgement and the Catalog's cohort list. The PGS Catalog's 'Spain' ('The Spanish study (University Hospital of Bellvitge, Hospital of Leon)') is the colorectal cancer case-control study that COHO already has as CRCGEN (COHO:0000585, Colorectal Cancer Genetics & Genomics). CRCGEN's own paper (PMC8574048) says its second component 'was conducted in parallel in the University Hospital of Bellvitge and in the Hospital of León, León, during 2007–2015', exactly the two hospitals the Catalog names, and the PGS Catalog paper PMID:31866242 acknowledges 'CRCGEN: Colorectal Cancer Genetics & Genomics, Spanish study' (COHO:0000585 already carries that phrase as a synonym). The other Spanish sample in that score (EPICOLON, Hospital Clínic Barcelona) has its own Catalog id. Add the Catalog name as a synonym and 'Spain' as an acronym of COHO:0000585 (no other COHO term uses 'Spain' as an acronym, so no editor note is needed); obsolete placeholder COHO:0002403 in its favour. Replaced by COHO:0000585 (Colorectal Cancer Genetics & Genomics), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002403 "obsolete The Spanish study (University Hospital of Bellvitge, Hospital of Leon)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002403 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

