# Individual: coho:COHO_0002451 (obsolete Texas-GWA study)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002451 coho:COHO_0000874)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002451 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. 'Texas-GWA study' is the name other groups (ICR's UK lung cancer GWAS papers) gave to the MD Anderson lung cancer GWAS of Amos et al. 2008: 1,154 ever-smoking European-ancestry lung cancer cases and 1,137 frequency-matched controls from Houston. That is exactly COHO:0000874 'MD Anderson Cancer Center lung cancer study' (definition from PMID:18385676: 1,154 cases and 1,137 controls from Houston, Texas). Add 'Texas-GWA study' as a synonym and the Catalog id 'Texas' as an acronym (no other COHO term uses 'Texas' as an acronym). Obsolete placeholder COHO:0002451 in its favour. Note COHO:0000874 already shares the acronym MDACC with COHO:0000875 (melanoma). Replaced by COHO:0000874 (MD Anderson Cancer Center lung cancer study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002451 "obsolete Texas-GWA study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002451 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

# Individual: coho:COHO_0002452 (Twin families EBNA-1 genome-wide association study)

