# Individual: coho:COHO_0002497 (obsolete Universitäts Klinikum Bonn)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002497 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UKBonn ('Universitäts Klinikum Bonn') is the PGS Catalog's id for the Lynch syndrome carriers from the University Hospital of Bonn in the Dueñas 2023 polygenic-score study: 547 people with genetically confirmed Lynch syndrome from 392 families, index patients and relatives found by cascade testing at Bonn's Institute of Human Genetics. The paper names them only by the hospital ('the UKB LS cohort'). No study name, design paper or registry name is given, and the paper does not say whether they come from the German HNPCC Consortium registry. It is a hospital's patient series, so, like HZ, it is not a cohort. No COHO term for a Bonn Lynch syndrome series (the Bonn terms in COHO are COVID, OMNI and psychiatric studies). The Spanish half, ICO (E522, placeholder COHO:0001901, 'the ICO LS cohort' from the Catalan Institute of Oncology's Lynch Syndrome Database), is a separate row. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002497 "obsolete Universitäts Klinikum Bonn"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002497 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

